     include publishing or mirroring the source code to other
     locations.
  c. Make personal copies of the source code.
  d. Modify this software and create derivative works.
  e. Use the original or modified software, in source or compiled form,
     for your own purposes, whether personal, educational, or commercial,
     within your own organization.
